uid "5d5626a2-9938-5097-90ed-3e9019e50489" :question/math-academy-id "q-142357" :question/problem "$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\bbox[3pt,white,border: 2px solid Gainsboro]{\\phantom{WW}} &={R}^{n} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* states the following: \n\n*Let $A$ be an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Then we have the following equivalence:*\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\color{blue}\\text{Col}(A)} &=\\mathbb{R}^{n} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $\\text{Col}(A).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272338 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07f8d9af-560e-5e04-801f-49c3569ea09a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464240} {:answer/id #uuid "3683cdbb-cea0-5d3a-88ae-46bbf35523a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464241}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186464240} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d8b8cb5-e75e-518a-91a0-160dae2c2bc4" :answer-field/key "$\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465054} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bba33a3-e841-5573-8abf-90651ed20a6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464242} {:answer/id #uuid "0c34db9f-4df3-5319-9c26-896a5b27e435" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464243}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186464242} :answer-field/id #uuid "05d917c1-327f-5ee0-8aed-ef99e81a107b" :answer-field/key "$A$ is  invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465055} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de2f17c6-86e7-560e-b3af-0ab0f7aab9fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464244} {:answer/id #uuid "06de2a3a-d315-52ff-898b-03d434ea28ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464245}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186464245} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bcd47e5-e550-5069-9017-2362f6f7a623" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {\\mathbb{R}}^{5}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465056} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8b9a6c1-79fd-5562-8398-adba35e81c9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668405} {:answer/id #uuid "f88e71c7-5960-5f2a-a7d0-17103c6e974f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668406}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186668405} :answer-field/id #uuid "e72880f3-4982-5638-a596-d216bcce961d" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668780}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0c320bbb-0961-56b0-99e4-beaa75aa8f10" :question/math-academy-id "q-142358" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\right\\}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{5} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=5=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0$ is false. Since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\left\\{{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\right\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is  invertible” is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{5}$ is true. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{5}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{5}$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272347 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4ec697a-de36-58b0-a09b-ffb9c847aeff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449652} {:answer/id #uuid "78fdbd67-166e-573c-b77c-2875405073f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449653}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186449652} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4acbd25-fc0e-5df4-a5a0-9e2908a9bffc" :answer-field/key "$\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450780} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb540fd1-edb6-5d6c-ba67-f5731cd79a1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449654} {:answer/id #uuid "436ef14f-26d4-5b22-b36f-ed6da6246439" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449655}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186449654} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c9e25d7-83f7-5d4a-9ef5-64e221fc60a5" :answer-field/key "$A$ is invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450781} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5d749ec-8e32-58f1-997a-3d7c01f317b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449656} {:answer/id #uuid "93874984-dcb6-5b93-8915-727ca84b807f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449657}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186449657} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1cc353b-858d-567c-919c-e053dd74f9d8" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)<4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450782}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4927fd87-c83e-52d3-b9bb-877110a8c514" :question/math-academy-id "q-142474" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\right.\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{4} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1$ is false. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is invertible” is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement $\\text{rank}(A)<4$ is true. Indeed, since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 4,$ or equivalently $\\text{rank}(A)<4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{rank}(A)<4$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272348 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d248bbb6-50b4-5d61-a95e-58f318131503" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464246} {:answer/id #uuid "7e5d0dfe-318f-5100-ac82-83455377b98c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464247}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186464247} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d37791a-a285-5a2f-af41-bcd2d8afc075" :answer-field/key "$A$ is invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465057} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3957e353-c39b-5011-af11-d2c9b6787af4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464248} {:answer/id #uuid "8a540690-cbd6-5a7b-8e6a-735ce1ef7a6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464249}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186464248} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cfe4de2-b1c4-55bb-a60d-27c7be7257dc" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)<n$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465058} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f6788d6-5506-57b7-9972-0d793d0b67f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464250} {:answer/id #uuid "67197e1a-6b46-5a73-9b9e-21d0f7711026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464251}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186464251} :answer-field/id #uuid "41d8c4a3-f095-50cd-bcf7-92ff6b429b75" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(A)={\\mathbb{R}}^{n}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465059}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "795129ab-7204-5692-a97c-e32525213e2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-142475" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then  $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{n} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=n=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $A$ is invertible.* $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, according to the invertible matrix theorem, \n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A).$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)<n.$* $\\,\\times$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$*  $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$A$ is invertible”; $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272349 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a86c9ea-79e9-50fc-bc35-cf2fee7cdfed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464252} {:answer/id #uuid "8712eb23-d6cb-5de9-b4b0-12bf3d790d49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464253}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186464252} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8ef167d-4bc6-5f6b-9cd2-3492c740a0f5" :answer-field/key "$det(A)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465060} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6eae4da1-dd85-56d5-8efd-a6744dd9efb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464254} {:answer/id #uuid "915b008a-1011-5090-8324-7e9001f057b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464255}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186464254} :answer-field/id #uuid "b38b7760-7c88-5d50-8e1a-83c437c15443" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(A)={\\mathbb{R}}^{16}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465061} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "952b73be-fa27-5c33-ac51-fe0f11cb7be4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464256} {:answer/id #uuid "3fc948d7-8345-54f5-aac4-3efcd42070c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464257}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186464257} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf6398a3-5006-54e1-b7af-c62ec5fc9eea" :answer-field/key "$A$ has $8$ pivot columns" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465062}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7036dc73-9ca4-59f2-b983-11eaacfb5a4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-142476" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$ .*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $A$ is an $8\\times 8$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{8} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=8=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $det(A)=0$* $\\,\\times$  \n\nSince the matrix $A$ is invertible, it must be  $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then  $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{16}.$*  $\\,\\times$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{8}.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $A$ has $8$ pivot columns.* $\\,✓$ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=8,$ which means that $A$ has exactly $8$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$A$ has $8$ pivot columns” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317166 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0373b669-29cd-5c16-8bc6-f02ee7222dbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315137} {:answer/id #uuid "1010c872-1dbe-5ad7-aa5e-04bf801caf2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315215} {:answer/id #uuid "5bcc56b2-3f31-58e4-b7df-97c4e5d7ba00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315641} {:answer/id #uuid "fca4573c-fd77-51c7-a278-367a2a4368b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316531} {:answer/id #uuid "fd8d6616-4916-5fe9-887f-0c8f19cd70f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316536}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316531} :answer-field/id #uuid "491bf6ee-6889-5481-aa4d-ef6f66809b5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316715}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c73928d-449b-56dc-94fe-ffe1e5cb8e3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-34166" :question/problem "If $p=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $q=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$, then $p\\cdot q=$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the dot product, we add up the products of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}+{p}_{2}\\cdot {q}_{2}+{p}_{3}\\cdot {q}_{3}+{p}_{4}\\cdot {q}_{4}+{p}_{5}\\cdot {q}_{5} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot 2+4\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 4+3\\cdot (-3)+(-2)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-10-4-4-9-10 \\\\  & =-37\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317169 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7aaa3b26-667c-55ba-9999-e8ed74ac7283" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315801} {:answer/id #uuid "8cb09cd4-9aec-5301-b698-a595d42372e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315903} {:answer/id #uuid "a56550ee-87d2-53db-bc3d-28dbd6881fab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316051} {:answer/id #uuid "bc508a1c-89f1-5f49-ae8b-8415dd9e70ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316182} {:answer/id #uuid "ea3130cf-9f6e-5fa9-b880-43d6416b03ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316420}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316051} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8c0803f-3f95-5cce-adfc-3107ba7971fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316938}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b9fb100e-a0ce-5519-bd8a-5ba4a8438726" :question/math-academy-id "q-34169" :question/problem "Let $u=\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}^{4} \\\\ 4 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}$ and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}^{-2} \\\\ -8x \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ If $u\\cdot v=12$ and $x<6$, find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Starting from the equation $u\\cdot v=12,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $x$ and then solve for $x$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =12 \\\\ 2{x}^{4}\\cdot 2{x}^{-2}+4\\cdot (-8x)+12\\cdot 4+6\\cdot 2 & =12 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-32x+48+12 & =12 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-32x+48 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-8x+12 & =0 \\\\ (x-2)(x-6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe get two solutions, ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=6.$ Since we need $x<6$, our final answer is $x=2$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317226 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d764ef8-ad33-5599-8778-a5c08551d497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315200} {:answer/id #uuid "1a120c7e-3eb5-5dbb-92c5-6cbd624e970f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315268} {:answer/id #uuid "444c9c69-dc48-516d-935a-0351dceff4f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315518} {:answer/id #uuid "9e32efc5-847e-5deb-b5d8-281622f6e605" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316005} {:answer/id #uuid "a44774b6-485f-5762-82b6-6e481402508b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316047}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315518} :answer-field/id #uuid "b46aa02f-87d3-5923-830c-977c9ef8cc09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316969}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f7a239b6-dd51-5d53-9de7-cf5ae156bb2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-34226" :question/problem "Let $r=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $s=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find $r+s.$" :question/worked-solution "We add the vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r+s & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4+1 \\\\ 2+5 \\\\ -3+2 \\\\ 1-8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317387 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c54bd68b-fc18-5fa5-9549-c756f4316346" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316229} {:answer/id #uuid "ce85b2ce-22b8-5663-a627-e9ec08bcf374" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316284} {:answer/id #uuid "d7dc61ab-394e-5368-9fc5-5027e5996acf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316323} {:answer/id #uuid "f1fa3072-d23b-507c-8036-22ce3c9d6957" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316465} {:answer/id #uuid "fc033ace-5f03-5bed-a981-059a775d2eb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316528}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316284} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffc19d80-f24e-5e44-827e-695e517d3044" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317155}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3d4fd42f-c149-5d08-9017-63ceab4faba9" :question/math-academy-id "q-34332" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$ and the vector $b=\\begin{bmatrix}k \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}k \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}k+9 \\\\ 2k+18\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}k+9 &=0 \\\\ 2k+18 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=-9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317441 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3de74079-f3cf-5def-aa1f-da3bc1be2fc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315476} {:answer/id #uuid "635f68a6-04d1-59e7-961c-48cb02bb94b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315676} {:answer/id #uuid "8118e81d-84eb-5f5d-8914-ed2e08788b0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315829} {:answer/id #uuid "dc334c09-7d2c-58fc-8e10-b27547ac5d85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316344} {:answer/id #uuid "f23e33d1-49d6-51b0-8d86-dbaead63b9d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316468}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315676} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe0284c0-67f8-5e76-ad83-63edd1004483" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317152}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0d4cb2fe-d794-5b24-afd6-08f39ce18357" :question/math-academy-id "q-34384" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors ${b}_{1}$, ${b}_{2}$, ${b}_{3}$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\text{Null}(A)?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -10 \\\\ 9 & 15\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A)$ if $Ab=0.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -10 \\\\ 9 & 15\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 90\\end{bmatrix}\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -10 \\\\ 9 & 15\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-59 \\\\ 118 \\\\ -33\\end{bmatrix}\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -10 \\\\ 9 & 15\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 180\\end{bmatrix}\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, none of the vector lies in $\\text{Null}(A).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317454 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6572e448-2a1b-54fa-b7eb-b164a363dfcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\,:\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430957} {:answer/id #uuid "77ade1d1-f580-5223-b0a2-1bf51cbff285" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430959} {:answer/id #uuid "9e92c0f2-12f6-52e4-bc39-5f630e281daf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430962} {:answer/id #uuid "b0b063f1-874e-516d-844c-6910584fd9fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ -3{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\,:\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430964} {:answer/id #uuid "bd56a073-7763-5f3e-8627-e620cdb34e7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{0\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430966}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430966} :answer-field/id #uuid "7741c95a-c056-57b4-9397-7a01a1ba8764" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316831}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "870e5cfd-95f3-5e52-b251-41fd48145e5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-34392" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe second equation tells us that ${x}_{2}=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that $x=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ is the only solution to this system.\n\nTherefore, $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318978 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52f930df-5902-5656-9330-9dcf0b91d57b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317843} {:answer/id #uuid "62a71865-052d-5dac-9440-faf1605c3338" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -\\frac{8}{3}\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317900} {:answer/id #uuid "a4ec4432-c14a-50c1-8b67-eb4182e2d2fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -\\frac{8}{3}\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318132} {:answer/id #uuid "c9167eb4-a9fb-5516-88f9-58d571fbaf2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318227} {:answer/id #uuid "f9b6cce5-a0db-57ca-9aef-dcc42629cbce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318397}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317843} :answer-field/id #uuid "69a6bce2-80ff-5b4f-83a3-86473d89bc46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318652}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bdf77374-96bf-579c-a597-3f47425959ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-34513" :question/problem "Given the matrix \n$G=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -\\frac{8}{3}\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find a basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(G).$" :question/worked-solution "In order to find a basis of $\\text{Col}(G),$ we reduce the matrix $G$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -\\frac{8}{3}\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 2 & -\\frac{8}{3}\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}^{′} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, only the $1$st column is a pivot column, while the $2$nd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nRemember that we need to pick the pivot columns from the *original matrix*, not from the reduced one. \n\nThe $1$st column from the original matrix is ${g}_{1}.$ So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(G)$ is ${{g}_{1}},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB={\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318982 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aa456ff-14e6-5b4c-8bb6-5fa53d7a73e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423601} {:answer/id #uuid "1b239761-1533-5b95-9abe-da3e7f8edb7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423602} {:answer/id #uuid "2b80385e-3a37-5b43-b815-d32cf7c3607c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423603} {:answer/id #uuid "79611b73-f06c-516d-a314-79fc8a0df50a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423607} {:answer/id #uuid "ce207c25-42d3-5952-b1ac-04aeb42aad0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423616}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423602} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb5ef360-4ae2-56e4-8b56-8bb54c7ef0fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318917}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "28419572-5f5f-5d91-aa00-334d8b1c45ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-34514" :question/problem "Given the matrix \n$F=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find a basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(F).$" :question/worked-solution "In order to find a basis of $\\text{Col}(F),$ we reduce the matrix $F$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 19\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $2$nd columns are pivot columns.\n\nRemember that we need to pick the pivot columns from the *original matrix*, not from the reduced one. \n\nThe $1$st and $2$rd columns from the original matrix are ${f}_{1}$ and ${f}_{2}.$ So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(F)$ is $\\{{f}_{1},{f}_{2}\\},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319314 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d0064e2-7095-50a4-9f68-f09ccda97572" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450548} {:answer/id #uuid "87590c0b-b8a7-56c3-9915-4df9e724e9df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450549}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186450549} :answer-field/id #uuid "71819ef2-7ff5-5f57-beb5-0822cdadf30b" :answer-field/key "If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451228} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a417e97-6614-5b7a-935f-3f703efe4728" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450550} {:answer/id #uuid "705d803b-01fe-5cbc-9e39-520b711450ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450551}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186450551} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd4d11a6-d574-56be-a1ff-bf51d5086a53" :answer-field/key "If $B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=2.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451229} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b9dcaeb-747d-5dcd-9605-08aa07e4d4fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450552} {:answer/id #uuid "7e2164d5-f2d9-5323-8150-cf625cddb533" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450553}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186450552} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d6cdc8f-65c5-5192-ac5b-16ea774e5f9b" :answer-field/key "If $C=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(C))=3.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451230}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6b1d1e88-f02a-5243-9bdc-9d244b4db578" :question/math-academy-id "q-34902" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement “If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1.$” is true. The matrix $A$ has $1$ pivot column and $1$ non-pivot column. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement “If $B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=2.$” is true. The matrix $B$ has $1$ pivot column and $2$ non-pivot columns (namely, the $2$nd and $3$rd columns). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement “If $C=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(C))=3.$” is false. The matrix $C$ has $3$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1.$”; “If $B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=2.$” only."}]}
